rthy and other prominent pentagon  officials  miller patel and mccarthy have all been  viewed as crucial witnesses for  understanding the government response to  the riots and former president trump's  reaction all three were involved in the  defense department's response to sending  national guard troops to the capitol as  the riot was unfolding there is no  suggestion that the officials themselves  erased the records  oh boy  oh boy  everyone involved who committed a crime  should be in jail or prison i'm not  saying  imprison people without due process and  without finding them guilty that's not  what i'm saying i'm saying they there  should be no  exempt exemptions here because of  people's roles whether it be in dod or  wherever the case may be  every day criminals  get in trouble all the time for  destroying evidence  white-collar criminals  often when it comes to tampering with or  destruction of evidence  end up in a situation where prosecutors  go ah it's really hard to prove that  they acted intentionally  gonna be very difficult to prove state  of mind here and yet we know it's not  that difficult because everyday  criminals street criminals as they are  sometimes called  get in trouble regularly for these exact  same things and there are just too many  coincidences here to believe that this  was not some kind of concerted effort  now you might recall  that days before what was ultimately the  final the last and final january 6th  committee hearing there was the idea  that on a beautiful tuesday the house  committee was going to get  recovered text messages from these  tranches of text messages that were  deleted  and  hours before the deadline  the revelation was  not recoverable not going to get them  sorry  and every aspect of this raises  questions as to in which organizations  were there  foot soldiers for lack of a better term  for the trump riot cover-up now we can't  say that secrets so part of this is  related to secret service here we're  talking about dod  i'm not ready to say  secret service was involved  but the longer it goes it starts to get  weird because on the one hand we have  secret service agents who supposedly  said in the aftermath of cassidy  hutchinson's devastating testimony about  what happened on january 6 we're willing  to come in and testify under oath about  all the lies cassidy hutchinson was  telling and i said at the time well  great get them under oath but then we'll  have competing under oath statements  until then all we have is nonsense and  then they never testified and the house  committee was welcoming them with open  arms and they never testified that  starts to get a little bit weird  then we hear well the text messages  involving the secret service also aren't  recoverable we can't give you anything  sorry  okay it starts to get a little weird now  we find out that the dod was wiping  phones  starting to get even weirder so i'm not  pretending to have an answer i'm not  positing any particular allegation of a  conspiracy i'm merely saying there's too  many coincidences here to believe that  this is merely a coincidence and there  seem to be actors in multiple  organizations at multiple agencies in  multiple levels of this  who don't seem to be forthcoming in the  way that you would imagine and that you  would hope government officials would be  that's where i will leave it and the  speculation can sort of go from there if  you have an idea as to what you believe  took place here find me on twitter at  deepakman and let me know who was  involved  and to what extent

